INT. WRESTLING WEIGH-IN SAUNA - PRE-DAWN

Cedar benches. A single bulb. Steam hangs thick enough to hold a handprint.

KWAME ASANTE, 20s, towel over his head, sits hunched, elbows on knees. SOLVEIG HAUG, 40s, his cornerman, perches across from him with a digital scale in her lap. Neither looks up.

KWAME
What's it say?

SOLVEIG
Hundred and fifty-four point eight.

KWAME
Limit's one-fifty-four.

SOLVEIG
I can read, Kwame.

KWAME
Then it's four-tenths of a pound.

SOLVEIG
It's four-tenths of a pound.

KWAME
Your mother's in the stands today.

SOLVEIG
Don't.

KWAME
I'm only saying.

SOLVEIG
Sweat.

KWAME
Four more minutes?

SOLVEIG
Six.

KWAME
You said four.

SOLVEIG
I say what the scale says.

KWAME
Last time, you said the scale lied.

SOLVEIG
Last time, you ate a banana.

KWAME
It was a small banana.

SOLVEIG
It was a banana, Kwame.

KWAME
Everybody's gonna look at me when I step up. All of them.

SOLVEIG
They look at everybody.

KWAME
You're not scared?

SOLVEIG
I'm warm.

KWAME
That's not an answer.

SOLVEIG
It's the only one I've got at five a.m.

KWAME
Give me the scale.

SOLVEIG
Not yet.

KWAME
Solveig.

SOLVEIG
Four minutes. Then I give it to you.

KWAME
You said six.

SOLVEIG
Then six.

He pulls the towel lower. She sets the scale on the bench between them and wipes her palm on her knee. Steam rolls over them both.
